From fc5f1fc8a389e125e7d5f979f7b88a2708d161ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: osy <osy@turing.llc>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:32:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] triton: give pixel shaders full coverage under
 target-independent rasterization

With a rasterizer ForcedSampleCount of N > 1 and single-sample render
targets bound, a pixel shader's vCoverage holds the pixel's N-sample
coverage.  The host backends rasterize such a draw at one sample, so
vCoverage arrived as 0x1.  DWM builds the window-shape mask it cuts out
of every drop shadow this way, XORing vCoverage into an R16_UINT target
so overlapping fan triangles cancel; the mask came out set wherever the
fan reached, and the cut-out erased the whole shadow.  Windows 11 drew
no window shadows on either D3DMetal or DXMT.

Under that state, bind in place of a PS that reads vCoverage a copy that
reads the constant (1 << N) - 1 instead: the coverage resolved at the
pixel centre, since the PS runs only where that one sample is covered.
The copy rewrites each vCoverage operand as a one-component immediate in
the code chunk, which tritonBuildDxbc places last, so the container ahead
of it is kept as is.  A shader that reads vCoverage inside a relative
index, or uses an encoding the operand walker does not know, keeps the
original PS.  One copy is made per ForcedSampleCount on first use and
kept on the shader, a failed attempt included, and a rasterizer or
render-target change rebinds the PS only when the one the draw needs
differs from the one last sent.  Draws without render targets
(UAV-only rendering) keep the original PS.

triton_dxbc_test gains a ps_5_0 case with an SV_Coverage input and
double immediates, checked by operand census, fxc disassembly of the
copy and a second pass that finds nothing left to replace.

Window shadows now render on D3DMetal and DXMT, matching pixel for pixel
a host-side substitution of DWM's mask shader.  Old/new A/B, GT1 fps:
Time Spy 29.91/30.06, Fire Strike 78.28/80.44, Fire Strike DXMT
48.23/48.20.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
